      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext"
        },
        "content": "<div style=\"font:13px/1.55 -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;color:#c7d0d9;background:#181b1f;border:1px solid #2c3235;border-left:3px solid #37872D;border-radius:3px;padding:12px 16px;\"><b style=\"color:#e8eaed\">Golden-recipe alignment for the IREN_MKZ GB300 fleet.</b><br>A <i>config baseline</i> is one distinct combination of chassis model, BIOS version, BIOS date, kernel release and OS release. The golden recipe wants exactly <b>one</b> baseline across the estate. Tray rows come from the on-tray <code>node-exporter</code> (<code>node_dmi_info</code>, <code>node_uname_info</code>, <code>node_os_info</code>); switch rows from the <code>switch-fw</code> exporter, which probes every switch hourly and is <i>not</i> filtered by the tray pickers above. Switch <i>availability</i> and IMEX faults live on the worklists board.<div style=\"font:12px/1.5 -apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;color:#8e8e8e;margin-top:8px\">ClusterMinder&nbsp;/&nbsp;CVT: <a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/nvis-l2-cvt-clusterminder/x\">Open worklists</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/cvt-clusterminder-inventory/x\">Inventory &amp; coverage</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/cvt-clusterminder-config/x\">Firmware &amp; config alignment</a>&nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;<a style=\"color:#6cc2ff\" href=\"/d/cvt-cable-validation/x\">Cable &amp; Layer-1 vs golden</a></div></div>",
        "mode": "html"
      },
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
